course: dictionary
lesson: 610
title: Awkwardness
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Awkwardness is a noun. Its main meaning is the uncomfortable feeling you get when you are embarrassed, especially around other people. Look at the clues in the sentence: «Polite words like "perspire" or "an upset stomach" sound clean; jokes like "Delhi belly" or "technicolour yawn" laugh the awkwardness away.»
explain: Some topics, like sweating or feeling ill, can make people feel embarrassed. The writer says polite words make these topics sound clean, and jokes laugh the embarrassment away. So awkwardness is the uncomfortable feeling that people try to get rid of.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does «laugh the uncomfortable feeling away» still make sense? Yes, so awkwardness means embarrassment here. Awkwardness can also mean clumsiness or being difficult to deal with, so always read the words around it to choose the right meaning.
fact: Awkwardness means the uncomfortable feeling of being embarrassed, especially in a social situation.
fact: Awkwardness can also mean clumsiness, or not moving easily and smoothly.
fact: Awkwardness can mean something is difficult to deal with.
fact: «Perspire» is a polite word for sweat.
fact: «Delhi belly» and «technicolour yawn» are jokes. They laugh at a topic so that people feel less embarrassed about it.
exercise: «Polite words like "perspire" sound clean.» What does perspire mean? | To yawn loudly | *To sweat | To shout with laughter | To fall asleep
exercise: Ben's face turned red, and nobody knew what to say. What is the awkwardness in this silence? | A loud noise | Being difficult to deal with | Clumsy movement | *An embarrassed, uncomfortable feeling
exercise: A teenager growing fast often has an awkwardness in how they move. What does awkwardness mean here? | *Clumsiness, not moving smoothly | Being very old | Loud singing | Speed of running
test: «Polite words like "perspire" sound clean; jokes laugh the awkwardness away.» What does awkwardness mean here? | The sound of a loud laugh | A brightly coloured yawn | *The uncomfortable, embarrassed feeling | The feeling of being very hungry
test: Which phrase in the sentence is a joke? | Polite words | Perspire | An upset stomach | *Technicolour yawn
exam: Kiran's first day at a new school was full of awkwardness. What does awkwardness mean here? | *An uncomfortable, embarrassed feeling | Shouting loudly | Being very tall | Giving out light
